---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { data, fmt, fmtTime, href, modelLabels, modelSlug } from '../lib/data'

const rows = [...data.perf].sort((a, b) => a.model.localeCompare(b.model) || a.case.localeCompare(b.case))
const inproc = [...data.inproc].sort((a, b) => a.model.localeCompare(b.model) || a.suite.localeCompare(b.suite))
const inprocSuites = [...new Set(inproc.map((r) => r.suite))]
const inprocModels = [...new Set(inproc.map((r) => r.model))]
const machineName = (key: string) => data.machines.find((m) => m.key === key)?.chip ?? key
const classOf = (key: string) => data.machines.find((m) => m.key === key)?.class ?? ''
const cases = [...new Set(rows.map((r) => r.case))]
---

<Base
  title="Speed & memory"
  description="Each model freshly loaded, three runs per case. Load time and prompt speed come from the cold run; output speed is the median. Shown for the machine picked above; machines are never pooled."
>
  <h2>Ollama models</h2>
  <div class="controls">
    <select data-facet="speed" name="case" aria-label="Case">
      <option value="">All cases</option>
      {cases.map((c) => <option value={c}>{c}</option>)}
    </select>
    <select data-facet="speed" name="model" aria-label="Model">
      <option value="">All models</option>
      {modelLabels.map((m) => <option value={m}>{m}</option>)}
    </select>
    <span class="count" data-count="speed"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="scroll">
    <table data-table id="speed">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th data-sort="text">Model</th>
          <th data-sort="text">Case</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">Output tok/s</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">Prompt tok/s</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">Embeds/s</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">Loaded GB</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">GPU</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">Cold load s</th>
          <th data-sort="text">Machine</th>
          <th data-sort="text">Run</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.map((r) => (
            <tr data-case={r.case} data-model={r.model} data-machine={r.machine}>
              <td>
                <a href={href(`/models/${modelSlug(r.model)}/`)}>{r.model}</a>
              </td>
              <td>
                <code>{r.case}</code>
              </td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.decode_tps ?? -1}>{fmt(r.decode_tps)}</td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.prompt_tps ?? -1} title={r.prompt_cached ? 'Ollama reused the loaded model, so the prompt was cached' : undefined}>
                {r.prompt_cached ? <span class="muted">cached</span> : fmt(r.prompt_tps, 0)}
              </td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.embeds_per_s ?? -1}>{fmt(r.embeds_per_s, 0)}</td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.loaded_gb ?? -1}>{fmt(r.loaded_gb, 2)}</td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.gpu_pct ?? -1}>{r.gpu_pct === null ? '—' : `${Math.round(r.gpu_pct)}%`}</td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.load_s ?? -1}>{fmt(r.load_s)}</td>
              <td class="muted">{machineName(r.machine)} <span class="pill class">{classOf(r.machine)}</span></td>
              <td class="muted">
                {r.run.slice(0, 10)}
                {r.stale && <span class="pill stale">stale</span>}
                {r.busy.length > 0 && <span class="pill busy" title={r.busy.join('; ')}>taken under load</span>}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="note">
    Ollama 0.40.11 ignores the context size for the qwen3.5 models, so their 8K and 32K rows repeat the 4K load
    ("cached"). The gemma4:e4b loaded size is implausibly small and likely leaves out its per-layer embeddings.
  </p>
  <h2>In-process and local models</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Detectors, classifiers, embedders, perceptual hashes and the image editor run in this process, not in Ollama. Time is
    the median per image; load is the one-off model load; memory is the largest reading in the latest run.
  </p>
  <div class="controls">
    <select data-facet="inproc" name="suite" aria-label="Suite">
      <option value="">All suites</option>
      {inprocSuites.map((c) => <option value={c}>{c}</option>)}
    </select>
    <select data-facet="inproc" name="model" aria-label="Model">
      <option value="">All models</option>
      {inprocModels.map((m) => <option value={m}>{m}</option>)}
    </select>
    <span class="count" data-count="inproc"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="scroll">
    <table data-table id="inproc">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th data-sort="text">Model</th>
          <th data-sort="text">Suite</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">Per image</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">Load</th>
          <th data-sort="num" class="num">Memory</th>
          <th data-sort="text">Machine</th>
          <th data-sort="text">Run</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          inproc.map((r) => (
            <tr data-suite={r.suite} data-model={r.model} data-machine={r.machine}>
              <td>
                <a href={href(`/models/${modelSlug(r.model)}/`)}>{r.model}</a>
              </td>
              <td>
                <code>{r.suite}</code>
              </td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.per_image_ms ?? -1}>{fmtTime(r.per_image_ms)}</td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.load_ms ?? -1}>{fmtTime(r.load_ms)}</td>
              <td class="num" data-value={r.mem_mb ?? -1}>
                {r.mem_mb === null ? '—' : `${Math.round(r.mem_mb).toLocaleString('en-US')} MB`} <span class="muted">{r.mem_kind}</span>
              </td>
              <td class="muted">{machineName(r.machine)} <span class="pill class">{classOf(r.machine)}</span></td>
              <td class="muted">
                {r.run.slice(0, 10)}
                {r.stale && <span class="pill stale">stale</span>}
                {r.busy.length > 0 && <span class="pill busy" title={r.busy.join('; ')}>taken under load</span>}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="note">
    <strong>rss</strong> is the whole process's resident memory, so it includes the runtime and every image held, and is an
    upper bound for the model alone. <strong>peak</strong> (the image editor) is that program's own peak. A dash means the
    run did not report it (the hashes have no weights to load).
  </p>
</Base>
